<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agesilaus II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 444–360 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agesilaus II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> from about 400 to 360 BCE, during the period of Spartan supremacy after the Peloponnesian War. He campaigned against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, won at Coronea in 394 BCE during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corinthian-war">Corinthian War</a>, and led Sparta through its decline after the defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Leuctra</a> in 371 BCE. He died returning from service as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agesilaus-ii.jpg" alt="Agesilaus II" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry Marriott Paget · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CUH_Agesilaus_and_Pharnabazus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
